": "Fresh independent polling or a surge of Democratic outside spending in the Spokane media market could narrow the race toward Lean R.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Michael Baumgartner (R) is running."]}, "overview": "First-term Republican Michael Baumgartner seeks a second term in Washington's 5th District, a seat that leans Republican by about five points, against Democrat Carmela Conroy in a 2024 rematch. Baumgartner holds a decisive financial advantage, with roughly $954,000 on hand compared to Conroy's $75,000, and outside groups have spent modestly against him. Expert raters overwhelmingly place the race in the Safe or Likely Republican column, with one outlet at Lean Republican.\n\nAvailable polling is limited and dated, but a May live-caller survey showed Baumgartner ahead 53-47, and prediction markets price his win probability near 80 percent. The race is a rematch in a district that has favored Republicans recently, and Conroy would need a strong national environment and more resources to close the gap. The forecast expects Baumgartner to win by a mid-to-high single-digit margin.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0968, "margin": -8.12}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1087, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0951, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0945, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1116, "margin": -8.0}]}